import lemmas.Compiler.CompRunHintClass

/-!
# The case `%12` of `+run` (README Gaps 25)

`crLast` (door axis `144095121988648959`, 318 cells, the last case of the
`?-` of `crDol`) is `[11 [%toss c12Clue] c12Ind]` (`c12_eq`, nouns by
`tools/gen/runhint12.py`): a hint whose clue tests the nomm and never
crashes, around the body `c12Ind`, which has the pushes of the indirect call
(`CompRunTwo.lean`): `+simple-next`, `+kerf`, `r-path` then `r-ref` (two
`+re`), `+emit` of `[%spy r-ref r-path pro] %hop out`, `q` under
`(lazy-from-reg r-path)` to that block, `+past` over `p`, `p` under
`(lazy-from-reg r-ref)`, `+copy`.

* `cr_disp_n12`, `c12_head`: `crDol` on `[12 p q]` runs `c12Ind`.
* `c12KfM`, `runLCH_n12`: the model of the case from `+kerf` on.
* `c12_tail`, `c12_kf`: the pushes from the run of `q` and from `+kerf` on
  (the proofs of `cr2_tailLRH`, `cr2_kfLRH` with the `%spy` block and
  `+lazy-from-reg`, `ct_lfr_gate`).
* **`comp_run_n12H`**: the case on every goal with `GInv`, against `runLCH
  env snd true msup` at a rest predicate, from the `PartH` of `p` and `q`;
  `res_n12H` its `GRes`; **`partH_n12`**.
-/

